# cEDH Analyzer - Project Rules

## Project Overview

A modern terminal UI application for analyzing competitive EDH (cEDH) decklists. Built with Python 3.11+, Textual for the TUI, and uv for package management.

## User Feedback
In the case the user uses unclear/vague language that does not adhere to industry standard terms, ask for clarification, and suggest alternative wording to help user learn standard language.

## Architecture

### Application Flow
```
User Input (URL) → EDH16 Scrape → Moxfield Scrape → Preprocess → Basic Analytics → Win Rate Analytics → Clipboard
```

### Key Directories
| Path | Purpose |
|------|---------|
| `src/cedh_analyzer/` | Main application code |
| `src/cedh_analyzer/stages/` | Pipeline stage implementations |
| `src/cedh_analyzer/widgets/` | Custom Textual widgets |
| `.cedh_data/` | Runtime data and state (gitignored) |

### Core Modules
| Module | Responsibility |
|--------|---------------|
| `app.py` | Main Textual app, screens, modals |
| `config.py` | Constants, thresholds, defaults |
| `state.py` | State persistence, resume logic |
| `stages/base.py` | Stage base class and result types |

## Development Commands

```bash
